    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive +17% boost due to the matchup against Nick Martinez; the combination of a favorable hitter's park and a dynamic platoon advantage creates an elite ceiling. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a monster day against Rod\u00f3n, buoyed by an elite BvP history and the protection of the #2 spot. We are also closely tracking **Jackson Merrill** (75.27); while the matchup against Ober is standard, his score is bolstered by a high-efficiency stolen base environment against a slow-delivering pitcher, making him a critical weapon in our chase for SB category dominance.\n\nOur bench decision came down to **Dominic Smith** (38.84) versus the bottom-tier starters in our active lineup, but he ultimately failed to clear the \"marginal\" threshold. While **Dominic Smith** offers moderate utility, his projected platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter and his unfavorable spot at the bottom of the order made him an easy exclusion for today\u2019s aggressive lineup. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Drake Baldwin** (56.48); while he projects as an effective spark plug at the top of the order, his utility depends entirely on confirming that lead-off placement. With **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** all currently sidelined on the IL, our roster depth remains tested, but the core group\u2014including **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Coby Mayo**\u2014is optimized to maximize both raw output and the scarcity-driven needs of our 5x5 build.",
